===Etymology 1===
From {{der|en|fr|sulfate}}, from {{der|en|NL.|sulphatum}}, taken from the expression {{m|la|acidum sulphatum||sulfuric acid}}, from {{m|la|sulphatus}}, from {{der|en|la|sulphur||sulfur}}. The term was first used in 1787 by the French chemist [[:w:Louis-Bernard Guyton de Morveau|L. B. G. De Morveau]]. Equivalent to {{af|en|sulfur|-ate|alt1=sulf(ur)|id2=chemical|t2=salt or ester}}.<ref>{{R:svenska.se|saob}}</ref>

